Well, if sites with high basal area are frequently changing states between years then it is not surprising for colonization and extinction to be correlated.  This just means that sites are not staying open or closed for very long.  I suppose it could also indicate a problem with closure if your high basal area sites were truly always "occupied" in that the species was in the general area but was not available for detection in some years.  This is a common problem for birds, depending on the sampling design.

